# Studio design system — "Editorial Mono"

Source of truth: [docs/design/studio-artboards.pdf](docs/design/studio-artboards.pdf)
(12 artboards: now playing, library/artists/albums/genres, docking, accent seeds,
lyrics, playback & sound, appearance, album/artist detail). This file distills
those boards into values you can use directly in Dart. If a new screen isn't covered
here, open that PDF and match its feel — flat surfaces, hairline dividers, restrained
accent, serif display type — rather than inventing a new visual language.

## Look and feel, in one line

Light, warm, editorial. Serif display type for names/titles, sans for everything functional.
No rounded "cards" with drop shadows or colored left-borders, no heavy gradients, no emoji, no
default Material ripple/elevation look. Flat surfaces separated by 1px hairlines. The accent
color is used sparingly — on progress, active state, and selection only, never as a background
wash.

## Color model

All colors are authored in OKLCH (`lightness% chroma hue`) and converted to sRGB hex for
Flutter's `Color`. Keep both in code: the OKLCH comment is the design source of truth if a token
ever needs to be re-derived (e.g. a new accent hue).

### Light theme

| Token             | OKLCH                  | Hex       | Use |
|---|---|---|---|
| `bg`              | `oklch(97% 0.01 80)`   | `#F9F4EE` | app background |
| `ink`             | `oklch(20% 0.01 80)`   | `#181611` | primary text, transport icon fill |
| `inkMuted`        | `oklch(50% 0.02 80)`   | `#696257` | secondary text, timestamps, artist/album subtext |
| `inkMutedAlt`     | `oklch(55% 0.02 80)`   | `#787165` | italic captions, nav-icon default state |
| `hairlineStrong`  | `oklch(85% 0.01 80)`   | `#D1CDC7` | art-placeholder border, progress-track background, window-control dots |
| `hairline`        | `oklch(90% 0.01 80)`   | `#E1DDD7` | panel/section dividers (top bar, icon rail, side panels) |
