### Dark theme

Dark mode is a deliberate re-tuning, not a naive invert — the accent is brightened
(chroma 0.14, lightness 68%, vs. 0.12/55% in light) so it still reads clearly against a dark
background.

| Token             | OKLCH                   | Hex       | Use |
|---|---|---|---|
| `bg`              | `oklch(18% 0.005 80)`   | `#13110F` | app background |
| `ink`             | `oklch(93% 0.005 80)`   | `#EAE7E4` | primary text |
| `inkMuted`        | `oklch(62% 0.01 80)`    | `#898680` | secondary text, timestamps |
| `inkDim`          | `oklch(70% 0.01 80)`    | `#A29E98` | tertiary / lower-emphasis text |
| `inkBright`       | `oklch(80% 0.005 80)`   | `#BFBDBA` | transport icon stroke (unfilled state) |
| `hairline`        | `oklch(28% 0.01 80)`    | `#2B2823` | dividers |
| `hairlineAlt`     | `oklch(30% 0.01 80)`    | `#302D28` | progress-track background |
| `hairlineStrong`  | `oklch(32% 0.01 80)`    | `#36322D` | stronger separators (panel borders) |
| `artSwatch`       | `oklch(30% 0.03 60)`    | `#392A1E` | placeholder album-art fill |

### Accent — terracotta (default seed hue 30)

| Token                 | OKLCH                 | Hex       | Use |
|---|---|---|---|
| `accent` (light)      | `oklch(55% 0.12 30)`  | `#AC5346` | played-progress fill, scrubber handle, active nav icon, active list-row tick, current-track highlight |
| `accentHover` (light) | `oklch(45% 0.12 30)`  | `#8C352A` | hover/pressed state |
| `accentPressed`(light)| `oklch(35% 0.12 30)`  | `#6C170E` | active/darkest, rarely used directly |
| `accent` (dark)       | `oklch(68% 0.14 30)`  | `#E17363` | same roles, dark theme |

### Dynamic color / custom accent — the formula, not just the hue

Every accent — whether auto-extracted from album art (via `palette_generator` /
`material_color_utilities`) or picked by the user in Settings → Appearance — plugs into the
**same** tonal formula. Only the hue changes:

- Light mode: `chroma = 0.12`, `lightness = 55%`, hue = seed hue.
- Dark mode: `chroma = 0.14`, `lightness = 68%`, hue = seed hue.

Named preset hues used in the mockups (Settings swatches / theme showcase), all light-mode
`oklch(55% 0.12 <hue>)`:

| Name       | Hue | Hex (light) |
|---|---|---|
| Terracotta (default) | 30  | `#AC5346` |
| Ochre      | 85  | `#916A00` |
| Sage       | 140 | `#48823B` |
| Teal       | 200 | `#00858D` |
| Indigo     | 270 | `#576CB7` |

When implementing: derive the seed hue either from the dominant album-art color (auto mode) or
the user's chosen swatch (custom mode), then run it through the fixed chroma/lightness pipeline
above for both themes. Never let the user pick chroma/lightness directly — only hue.

## Typography

- Display / serif — **Spectral** (fallback `Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif`). Used only for:
  track titles on Now Playing (44px / weight 500 / line-height 1.05), album/artist names on
  detail pages, genre tile names, italic supporting lines (e.g. artist bio, "now playing" caption).
- UI / body — **Work Sans** (fallback `'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif`). Everything else:
  nav labels, list rows, tabs, sort/order controls, buttons, timestamps, mini-player text.
- Don't introduce a third typeface. Don't set Work Sans for anything that reads as a "name"
  (track/album/artist/genre) — that's Spectral's job, it's what gives the app its editorial feel.

## Layout conventions

- App shell: fixed 64px left icon rail (Library / Now Playing / Queue / Settings), separated
  from content by a `hairline` right-border. 44px top titlebar with 3 window-control dots
  (`hairlineStrong`), no OS-native chrome.
- Now Playing (hero) screen: centered content column, `max-width: 520px`. Optional right "Up
  Next" panel, fixed 280px, separated by a `hairline` left-border.
- Library screens (All/Artists/Albums/Genres): collapsible quick-nav sidebar, 168px wide, with a
  collapse chevron; tabs row for All/Artists/Albums/Genres/Playlists/Recently Added; sort/order
  controls are **typographic** (plain text + chevron), never boxed dropdown chips; column headers
  above the row list.
- Detail pages (Album/Artist): back breadcrumb, large art/photo, title block, Play All/Shuffle
  action row, then a plain track/album list. Currently-playing track shows a small equalizer
  icon in place of its track number, highlighted in `accent`.
- Flat surfaces only: no card backgrounds, no drop shadows except the ~1-3px shadow under the
  scrubber handle dot. Square corners on all internal elements; the outer app window itself is
  the only thing with rounded corners (20px, in the mockups).

## The persistent player bar — "divider-scrubber" pattern

This is the one component every screen with a footer player shares. Do not reinvent it per
screen.

1. A **20px-tall strip directly above the player bar**, edge-to-edge (no side padding — it is
   the visual seam between the main view and the bottom bar), containing:
   - a 2px hairline track (`hairlineStrong` light / `hairlineAlt` dark) spanning full width
   - an `accent`-filled portion from the left edge to the current playback position
   - a small circular handle dot (10px, `accent` fill, subtle drop shadow) sitting exactly on
     the played/unplayed boundary
   - elapsed/remaining time labels, small (11px, `inkMuted`), inset 20px from each edge
2. Below that, a flat **64px content row**, `space-between`:
   - left, fixed ~260px: 40px art thumbnail + title (ink) / artist (inkMuted)
   - center: transport icons only (shuffle, previous, play/pause, next, repeat), ~20px gaps,
     no progress bar embedded here
   - right, fixed ~130px: small volume cluster (speaker icon + a short 64–120px slider), same
     hairline-track-with-handle visual language as the main scrubber, just smaller

Do not stack transport icons above a separate progress bar, and do not squeeze the progress bar
and volume slider into the same row fighting for space — both were tried and explicitly rejected
in favor of the pattern above.

## Accent-usage discipline (read this before adding a splash of color anywhere)

Accent color is allowed on: played-progress fill, the scrubber/volume handle dots, the active
icon-rail item, the active sidebar entry's tick mark, the currently-playing track's highlight +
equalizer icon, and selection rings in the accent picker. It is not allowed as a button
background, a card background, a large surface wash, or a default icon color. When in doubt,
default to `ink`/`inkMuted` and reserve `accent` for "this is the thing that's active right now."
